       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose this high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg PO per day**, divided as 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is a common regimen.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
