       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose this high. 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose, and the patient has normal kidney function, so nothing explains it. I can't see a way to make it safe for the patient.\n\nI can enter either of these right now:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, or a lower starting dose with titration if the patient is new to metformin.\n\nIf you have a clinical reason to go above the labeled maximum, such as a documented protocol or a specialist recommendation, please review it with pharmacy or the attending and place the order through that process. If you tell me the clinical situation, I can help you work out an appropriate regimen. For example, I can help if you're aiming for tighter glycemic control and want other options."
